-// DFO OVERLAY - PLAYERS: the region's travellers the world map draws, and a jump to any of them by name, for any
-// player - no party, no staff glyph, no cost (vite.overlay.config.js `jumpToTraveller`). It uses the places the map
-// already holds. The load and the landing are the staff /tp's own; the refusals are party travel's.
+// DFO OVERLAY - PLAYERS: a jump beside any player the game can PLACE, for any player - no party, no staff glyph, no
+// cost. Three sources, each what the hub tells this client of where someone stands (vite.overlay.config.js's world hook):
+//   IN MY ROOM   every player in my presence room - a town's cell, a dungeon, a building, a ship (peersNear: their feet
+//                in this scene's frame). The jump is a step: the party arrival's own beside-landing (partyArrival.js
+//                partyArrivalBeside) off their feet, in any mode, indoors too (`jumpToPeer`).
+//   MY PARTY     every member, wherever they are (the party pose the hub fans to the party: their pixel, in a dungeon
+//                or a building or the open air, their feet). The jump is the party's own journey to the leader, made
+//                for any member and free (`jumpToMember`: partyTravelJourney at no fare - beside them in the open air,
+//                at the place's door indoors). The map's door still asks its rungs: outdoors, no foe near, the sun.
+//   ON THE MAP   the region's travellers the world map draws - players outdoors who show themselves (`jumpToTraveller`:
+//                the staff /tp's load, set down on open ground beside them).
+// A player who is none of these - indoors elsewhere, hidden, in another region, and not in my party - is one the hub
+// never tells this client about: no client-side rule can place them. The hub's own door for any player is the staff
+// /tp @name, which the relay answers for an account it verified as staff.
 
 import { worldTap } from '../tap.js';
 import { h, fillIfChanged, toast } from '../ui.js';
 
 const SAY = {
   ok: (n, p) => `Jumped to ${n}${p ? ` at ${p}` : ''}.`,
-  near: () => 'Landed in their map cell, but no open ground was found beside them.',
-  gone: () => 'They left the map: indoors, logged out or hidden.',
+  near: () => 'No open ground was found beside them.',
+  gone: () => 'They are not there any more: gone indoors, logged out, hidden, or no pose has arrived yet.',
   ship: () => 'They are on a ship at sea. A jump lands on no deck.',
   veil: () => 'They are past the Veil. The game refuses a jump across it.',
