+//   IN MY ROOM   every player in my presence room - a town's cell, a dungeon, a building, a ship (peersNear: their feet
+//                in this scene's frame). The jump is a step: the party arrival's own beside-landing (partyArrival.js
+//                partyArrivalBeside) off their feet, in any mode, indoors too (`jumpToPeer`).
+//   MY PARTY     every member, wherever they are (the party pose the hub fans to the party: their pixel, in a dungeon
+//                or a building or the open air, their feet). The jump is the party's own journey to the leader, made
+//                for any member and free (`jumpToMember`: partyTravelJourney at no fare - beside them in the open air,
+//                at the place's door indoors). The map's door still asks its rungs: outdoors, no foe near, the sun.
+//   ON THE MAP   the region's travellers the world map draws - players outdoors who show themselves (`jumpToTraveller`:
+//                the staff /tp's load, set down on open ground beside them).
+// A player who is none of these - indoors elsewhere, hidden, in another region, and not in my party - is one the hub
+// never tells this client about: no client-side rule can place them. The hub's own door for any player is the staff
